// A recipe, written from md-docs/recipes/markdown-pages.md by scripts/docsite/recipes.py;
// edit the recipe, not this file.
page RecipeMarkdownPages(path: "/recipes/markdown-pages", title: "Write a page as a Markdown file — Recipes", description: "To write a page in Markdown, put a `.md` file under `src/`.") {
    RecipeShell("Write a page as a Markdown file", summary: "To write a page in Markdown, put a `.md` file under `src/`. Its *front matter* — the lines between the two `---` lines at the top — names the page's attributes; the rest is the body.  This file is a docs page at `/guide/install`:  ````md --- path: /guide/install title: Installing description: Get wf on your machine in a minute. layout: DocsShell type: article image: /install.png image_alt: A terminal running wf build ---  # Installing  Download a release, or build from source:  ```sh cargo install webfluent ```  Then `wf init my-site`. ````  The front matter keys are the page's attributes:  | Key | Meaning | |---|---| | `path` | The route. Default: `/` for `index.md`, otherwise `/<file-name>` | | `title` | The page's title | | `description` | The snippet a search result shows | | `layout` | The component that frames the body | | `image` · `image_alt` | The link-preview image, and what it shows | | `type` | `website` (the default) or `article` | | `noindex` | `true` keeps the page out of search results and the sitemap | | `lang` | The language the page is written in, when it is not the site's: `en`, `ar`, `pt-BR` | | `translates` | The page this one is a translation of, by name: `About` |  The page's name is the file's stem, capitalised: `install.md` is the page `Install`. The body is placed as `Markdown(…)` in the page, inside the layout's default slot when the front matter names a layout.  ### Frame `.md` pages with a layout  `layout: DocsShell` frames the body in a component with a default slot — the same kind of component a `.wf` page names as its `layout:` ([Pages and routing](/docs/guide/pages-and-routing#layouts)):", outputs: [], since: "", recipes: RECIPE_INDEX, sections: [Anchor(id: "how-it-works", label: "How it works")], related: [RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Describe pages to search engines and link previews", to: "/recipes/search-and-link-previews"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Render Markdown", to: "/recipes/render-markdown"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Show code on a page", to: "/recipes/show-code")], source: "md-docs/recipes/markdown-pages.md", how: true, hasVariations: false) {
        code {
            CodeBlock(#"component DocsShell {
    slot
    Row(gap: .lg) {
        Sidebar {
            Sidebar.Item(to: "/guide/install") { Text("Installing") }
            Sidebar.Item(to: "/guide/pages") { Text("Pages") }
        }
        Container { children }
    }
}"#, title: "wf")
        }
        Markdown("A docs site is then a folder of `.md` files, one layout, and a `.wf` file for the `app`. (`wf docs` is something else: a gallery of every component the project can use — [CLI](/reference/cli#wf-docs).)")

    }
}
